sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch09-07> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The Second Law of Thermodynamics is an important and general principle but is not universally valid; many systems in nature behave like rule 37R and do not show a uniform trend toward increasing randomness.";
    dc:type "general-principle";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Second Law is general but not universally valid";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 9, “Fundamental Physics”; section “Irreversibility and the Second Law of Thermodynamics” (from p. 441), p. 457. Scope: physical, biological and other natural systems to which the Second Law is applied"
}
